## Top 5 This Week

1. **CaptiveCrunch / Midnight Blizzard:** A sub-cluster of Midnight Blizzard (Storm-2945) has been actively compromising hotel sign-in portals since May 2026 to deliver malware and steal credentials from travelers. If your org has traveling users or hospitality-sector partners, threat intel review and conditional access tightening for non-compliant or unfamiliar network locations is warranted now.

2. **Writeback for Cloud-Managed Remote Mailboxes hits GA:** If you are on the path to retiring your last on-premises Exchange server, this is the unlock you have been waiting for. Writeback is now GA across WW, GCCH, DoD, and 21Vianet, supporting up to 600,000 cloud-managed mailboxes per tenant. Start planning your Exchange attribute SOA migration.

3. **Copilot Domain Exclusion for web grounding is GA:** Admins can now block specific external domains from being used to ground Copilot responses. For organizations with compliance requirements around acceptable web sources, this is an actionable control you can configure today in the Microsoft 365 admin center.

4. **Trusted Launch as Default is GA for Azure Gen2 VMs:** New Gen2 VM deployments via Portal, PowerShell, and CLI already get Secure Boot and vTPM by default. If you use ARM templates, Bicep, Terraform, or SDKs, a one-time registration is required to extend this default to your IaC pipelines. Act on this before your next automated deployment cycle.

5. **CVE-2026-66803: Azure Cosmos DB RCE via improper access control:** An unauthenticated network attacker can execute code against Azure Cosmos DB. If your tenant or applications consume Cosmos DB, verify your exposure and apply any available mitigations from the MSRC advisory immediately.

