## Identity & Access

- **[Give Every AI Agent Its Own Identity](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/j8AGpZ8Z2yA)** [GA] - AI agents carry real identity risk: overpermissioned or hijacked agents can cause significant damage at machine speed. Microsoft Entra Agent ID assigns each agent its own unique, manageable identity so you can apply Zero Trust governance, visibility, and least-privilege controls to non-human actors the same way you do for users. Start inventorying deployed agents and plan to onboard them to Entra Agent ID.

- **[Writeback for Cloud-Managed Remote Mailboxes: Now Generally Available](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/exchange-team-blog/writeback-for-cloud-managed-remote-mailboxes-now-generally/ba-p/4543507)** [GA] - Writeback is GA across all environments (WW, GCCH, DoD, 21Vianet), supporting up to 600,000 cloud-managed mailboxes per tenant. This closes the final technical gap for organizations looking to retire their last on-premises Exchange server by transferring Exchange attribute Source of Authority to Exchange Online. Review the GA announcement and validate your Entra Connect Sync or Cloud Sync configuration before enabling.

- **[Microsoft Teams: View and manage auto attendant shared voicemails directly in the Queues app](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=567457)** [GA] - Auto Attendant voicemails will surface directly in the Queues app, giving contact center teams a single place to track, triage, and respond to customer messages without switching contexts. Arriving August 2026, verify Queues app permissions and voicemail routing policies are configured for affected Auto Attendants before rollout.

---

## Endpoint & Device Management

- **[What's New in Microsoft Intune - July](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-intune-blog/what-s-new-in-microsoft-intune-july/ba-p/4537392)** [GA] - July's Intune release centers on giving admins clearer visibility into device sync health and more confident control over fleet management at scale. Key highlights include demystified Windows device sync status to aid troubleshooting and improvements to compliance reporting. Review the full release notes and identify which new reporting capabilities can replace existing manual checks in your runbooks.

