## Collaboration & Productivity

- **[What's New in Microsoft Teams | July 2026](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-teams-blog/what-s-new-in-microsoft-teams-july-2026/ba-p/4542510)** [GA] - July's Teams release introduces the Meeting Recaps app for easier post-meeting catch-up, improved app and agent management controls for admins, and a range of AI-powered features across roles. Review the full post and assess whether any new app management policies need updating in the Teams admin center.

- **[What's New in Microsoft Teams | April 2026](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-teams-blog/what-s-new-in-microsoft-teams-april-2026/ba-p/4515907)** [GA] - April's release recap covers collaboration intelligence, hybrid meeting improvements, and calling enhancements. If you missed the M365 Community Conference announcements, this post consolidates what shipped in April and is worth reviewing to catch up on any features that may now be live in your tenant.

- **[What's New in Microsoft 365 Copilot | July 2026](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-365-copilot-blog/what-s-new-in-microsoft-365-copilot-july-2026/ba-p/4538332)** [GA] - July's Copilot update covers model upgrades, agent additions in Copilot Chat, push notifications in the Copilot app, new Cowork capabilities, Copilot Notebook reference support, Word workflows, and Power Platform skills. Review the release post to identify user-facing changes that need communication or training updates in your tenant.

- **[What's New in Microsoft Security: July 2026](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/07/30/whats-new-in-microsoft-security-july-2026/)** [GA] - July's security update roundup focuses on AI environment security, AI-assisted defense capabilities, and operational foundations for AI-powered security operations. Use this as your checklist to confirm which new Defender and Purview features are now available in your environment and require policy or configuration attention.

- **[Writeback for Cloud-Managed Remote Mailboxes: Now in Public Preview](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/exchange-team-blog/writeback-for-cloud-managed-remote-mailboxes-now-in-public/ba-p/4520138)** [Preview] - This is the original public preview post, superseded by GA as of August 3, 2026. Included for reference; if you were tracking the preview, the GA announcement is now the authoritative source. Customers still on the preview should confirm they meet the GA prerequisites and validate writeback behavior in their environment.

- **[From AI Experiments to Digital Workforce: Do Enterprises Need a Chief Agent Officer?](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-security-community/from-ai-experiments-to-digital-workforce-do-enterprises-need-a/ba-p/4542520)** [GA] - As agent fleets grow, governance accountability is fragmenting across IT, security, and compliance teams with no clear owner. This post frames the emerging organizational challenge and is useful context for engineering teams preparing governance frameworks or advising leadership on AI agent ownership models.

- **[SharePoint Showcase: 10 Custom AI Skills Every SharePoint Site Owner Should Build](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-sharepoint-blog/sharepoint-showcase-10-custom-ai-skills-every-sharepoint-site/ba-p/4535414)** [GA] - Copilot Skills in SharePoint let site owners define reusable natural language instructions that teach Copilot to perform repeatable team tasks, from meeting summaries to project briefs. These skills are persisted at the site level, making them a shared team asset. Consider whether your governance model needs guidance on who can create and publish skills within your SharePoint sites.

- **[Dataverse Plugin for Coding Agents: OpenAI and Codex Marketplace Expansion](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/blog/2026/07/28/dataverse-plugin-for-coding-agents-openai-and-codex-marketplace-expansion/)** [GA] - The Dataverse plugin is now available in the OpenAI and Codex marketplaces, extending developer access to Dataverse data from external coding agent environments. If your organization uses Dataverse for business data, review data access permissions and API governance policies to ensure external coding agent usage is accounted for.

- **[Microsoft Teams: See more messages on mobile](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=568067)** [GA] - A streamlined mobile messaging layout will display more content on screen with improved readability, making it easier to follow conversation flow in Teams on mobile. Rolling out September 2026, no admin action required but worth noting in any mobile UX change communications.

- **[Microsoft Teams: Updated header and dashboard for chats and channels on mobile](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=567461)** [GA] - A redesigned mobile header and lightweight dashboard surfaces key channel details, people, and pinned content in one place, aligning mobile and desktop navigation patterns. Rolling out September 2026, inform Teams Champions and helpdesk staff ahead of rollout.

- **[Microsoft Teams: Clearer text highlighting in dark mode](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=566858)** [GA] - Text highlighting when composing messages in dark mode will be visually consistent with other editing surfaces. Rolling out September 2026, no admin action required.

- **[Microsoft Teams: Teams shared display mode and peripheral detection available for DoD environments](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=567465)** [GA] - Shared display mode and BYOD peripheral detection for inventory management via the Pro Management portal are now available in DoD GCC environments. Rolling out August 2026; DoD environment admins should validate Pro Management portal access and peripheral detection policies.

- **[Microsoft Teams: Ability for IT admins to customize user notification messages for recording and transcription in calls](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=567302)** [GA] - Admins can now customize a portion of the notification messages users see when recording or transcription starts in Teams calls. Rolling out August 2026; review whether your legal or compliance team has requirements for the notification text and configure accordingly via Teams admin center calling policies.

- **[Microsoft Teams: Enhanced delegated calling with delegate call access restrictions and join notifications](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=567306)** [GA] - Delegators can now lock active calls to prevent delegates from joining or resuming, and can enable warning tones when a delegate joins. Rolling out August 2026; this is particularly relevant for executive and front-desk calling scenarios where call privacy is a requirement.

- **[Planner: Task Details Side Pane experience](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=566866)** [GA] - Task details now open in a side pane, keeping the Board, Grid, or My Tasks view visible while editing, eliminating the context-switch caused by modal dialogs. This shipped July 2026; no admin action required, but worth noting in productivity-focused user communications.

- **[SharePoint: Admin Center detailed report on Everyone except external user permissions](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=561038)** [GA] - SharePoint Advanced Management admins will get item-level detail on permissions granted to the "Everyone except external users" and "Everyone" special groups. Rolling out August 2026; run this report early to identify overshared content and close exposure gaps before it surfaces in an audit.

- **[Microsoft Teams: Unblock users to send messages while file is uploading in the background](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=560813)** [GA] - Asynchronous file uploads eliminate the blocking behavior that forced users to wait for large file transfers before sending messages. Rolling out August 2026, no admin action required.

- **[Microsoft Teams: Improved organization for muted and meeting chats](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=559605)** [GA] - Teams now auto-groups muted chats and can collect meeting chats into dedicated sections to reduce clutter in the chat list. Note: this feature was temporarily rolled back as of July 20, 2026. Monitor the roadmap item for reactivation before including it in user communications.

- **[OneDrive: Improved max path error experience on desktop](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=557563)** [GA] - When a file path exceeds the 520-character sync limit, OneDrive desktop will now show exactly how many characters are over the limit and guide users through renaming or moving the file. Rolling out August 2026; useful context for organizations with deep folder hierarchies or legacy naming conventions that frequently hit path limits.

