## AI & Copilot

- **[Why Ungoverned AI Agents Are Dangerous](https://www.youtube.com/shorts/XdgO2fjg3KQ)** [GA] - Overpermissioned AI agents with access to enterprise data and tools represent a high-impact attack path: a compromised agent can move at machine speed before anyone notices. This short from Microsoft Mechanics frames the governance risk clearly and is useful material for security architecture and leadership conversations about agent policy.

- **[The Next Measure of AI Momentum Is Work Transformed](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/blog/2026/07/30/the-next-measure-of-ai-momentum-is-work-transformed/)** [GA] - Microsoft 365 Copilot has surpassed 30 million paid seats with net seat adds more than doubling quarter over quarter. For engineering teams, accelerating seat counts mean governance, data access policy, and agent oversight frameworks need to scale with deployment; use this signal to pressure-test your current Copilot governance posture.

- **[Prompt Columns in GA: Turning Business Apps Data into Persisted AI Insights](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/blog/2026/07/29/prompt-columns-july2026/)** [GA] - Prompt Columns in Power Apps allows natural language prompts defined once to automatically generate and persist AI-produced classifications, summaries, and recommendations directly in Dataverse tables, with no code required. This is a new data-generation surface; ensure your data governance and DLP policies cover AI-generated content stored in Dataverse.

- **[Microsoft Viva: Viva Glint - Copilot admin configuration assistance](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=567320)** [GA] - A Copilot-powered conversational assistant embedded in the Viva Glint admin experience will answer configuration and how-to questions with deep links to relevant settings pages. Rolling out September 2026; limited to users with Viva Glint Admin permissions, no additional configuration required to enable.

