## Action Required

- **[CaptiveCrunch: Midnight Blizzard Active Campaign Against Travelers](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/07/31/captivecrunch-midnight-blizzard-targets-travelers-worldwide-for-malware-delivery-and-credential-theft/)** [GA] - Active threat, act now. Review and harden conditional access policies for sign-ins from hospitality or unknown network locations, enforce phishing-resistant MFA for all traveling users, and brief your SOC on the Storm-2945 indicators of compromise published in this advisory.

- **[CVE-2026-66803: Azure Cosmos DB Remote Code Execution](https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-66803)** [GA] - Unauthenticated network RCE against Cosmos DB warrants immediate review. Check your tenant and application dependencies on Cosmos DB, review the MSRC advisory for mitigation steps, and confirm any available platform-side patches or configuration controls are applied.

- **[Trusted Launch as Default: One-Time Registration Required for IaC Pipelines](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-security-community/secure-by-default-trusted-launch-as-default-is-now-generally/ba-p/4541672)** [GA] - Before your next automated Azure VM deployment: complete the one-time registration to enable Trusted Launch as Default for ARM templates, Bicep, Terraform, and SDK-based deployments. Without registration, IaC-provisioned Gen2 VMs will not inherit the new secure-by-default baseline.

- **[SharePoint Admin Center: Everyone Except External Users Permissions Report](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=561038)** [GA] - Arriving August 2026. Plan to run this report immediately upon availability to identify items shared broadly via the "Everyone except external users" group. Overshared content surfaced here should be remediated before your next internal or external audit cycle.

- **[Three Chromium CVEs in Edge: WebGL and GPU](https://msrc.microsoft.com/update-guide/vulnerability/CVE-2026-13032)** [GA] - CVE-2026-13032, CVE-2026-13030, and CVE-2026-13028 are addressed in the latest Microsoft Edge Chromium build. Verify Edge patch compliance across all managed endpoints in Intune or your patch management tooling; WebGL use-after-free vulnerabilities are high-risk for browser-based exploit chains.

