## Documentation Updates

**Identity & Access**

- **[SMS and Voice Retirement FAQ Split into Dedicated Page](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs/commit/938217238eb9520112ac2f6eafad1eac6c1b78d6)** - The SMS/voice authentication retirement FAQ has been moved to its own dedicated page, making it easier to find retirement timeline and migration guidance; relevant for any org still running SMS or voice as MFA methods.

- **[New Multitenant Architecture Guide Published](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs/commit/7eb64a786de183ec4cb0483b41187ac879813984)** - A new Entra ID multitenant architecture guide has been added, covering design patterns and decision points for organizations managing multiple tenants; reference this if you are designing or reviewing a multitenant Entra topology.

- **[Global Secure Access: Remote Network CPE Behind NAT Guidance Added](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs/commit/649f7a17c18170104e4cf9aae8c93ffac9fcf00f)** - New guidance documents how to configure remote network CPE devices sitting behind NAT for Global Secure Access, addressing a common deployment gap for branch office scenarios.

- **[Global Secure Access: Internet Access Profile Documentation Revised](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs/commit/73565b59f03b2578d8099cbc0d8525cccf829532)** - The Internet Access profile docs have been meaningfully rewritten; review if you are configuring or auditing Global Secure Access Internet Access policies.

- **[New Entra Zscaler ZIdentity Integration Tutorial](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/entra-docs/commit/0372550fa2b9824e825d48440331bd42e9ac880c)** - A new step-by-step tutorial for integrating Zscaler ZIdentity with Microsoft Entra ID has been published; relevant for organizations running Zscaler alongside Entra for identity-aware network access.

**Endpoint & Device Management**

- **[Microsoft Tunnel Prerequisites Updated](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/memdocs/commit/52b93b3a20cbcecd14913f209523bdf63ad7eb8c)** - Prerequisites for Microsoft Tunnel have been updated; review before deploying or upgrading Tunnel infrastructure to avoid configuration failures.

- **[CVE-2026-47301 Documented in Configuration Manager Console Extension Fix](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/memdocs/commit/6d50432a73a4967dc4acd5a400630bec719b552e)** - CVE-2026-47301 has been added to the Configuration Manager console extension KB article; if you manage ConfigMgr console extensions, review the referenced KB for remediation steps.

**Security & Compliance**

- **[Tenant Allow/Block List: Block Entry Behavior for Domains and Subdomains Clarified](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/defender-docs/commit/3e913ef1187a6ea001eb6df467970a007da91eb5)** - The documentation now clarifies exactly how block entries for domains and subdomains are evaluated in the Tenant Allow/Block List, resolving a common point of confusion about scope and inheritance behavior.

- **[IIJ Added as Trusted ARC Sealer](https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/defender-docs/commit/ba8a948070bbe3dd56f8d6211b7df43f9a8bcaaa)** - IIJ has been added to the list of trusted ARC sealers in Defender for Office 365 configuration guidance; relevant if IIJ is in your mail flow path and you are troubleshooting ARC authentication failures.